<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέχνως</span></b> , Adv. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτεχνος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without art, without rules of
				art, empirically,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.11.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				501a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτεχνῶς</span></b>  (with penult.
			short), Adv. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτεχνής,</span>
			<i>simply,</i> i.e. <i>really, absolutely,</i> freq. in Com., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἥκω παρεσκευασμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				408
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1174
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλὸν ἀ.</span>
			<i>simply</i> beautiful, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Av.</u>
				820
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. γε παμπόνηρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					106
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥύγχος ἀ. ἔσθ᾽ ὑός</span>
			<i>simply</i> a swine's snout, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				102
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μὲν οὖν σκύτη βλέπει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					282
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ τοῦ Ὁμήρου ἐπεπόνθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					198c
				</span></i>
			; <i>bona fide, sincerely,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμπου ἕνεκα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				6.20
			</span></i>: freq. in comparisons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὥσπερ</span>
			<i>just</i>
			like , <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				90c
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. οἷον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					952e
				</span></i>
			: with neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἂν διαλεχθείην γ᾽
				ἀ.</span> would <i>just</i> not have spoken a word to him,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				425
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. οὐδείς</span>
			<i>simply</i> no one, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Av.</u>
				605
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				362
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				288a
			</span></i>.—On <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέχνως</span> and
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νῶς</span>
			v. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				109
			</span></i>.</div>
